<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">08, Frequently Asked Questions</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Commercial washer repair, what SoCal operators ask us</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How much does commercial washer repair cost?</h3>
        <p>Commercial diagnostic is $120, applied to the repair if approved. Most repairs run $180–$500. Drain pump, motor coupling, door lock, door boot, or water inlet valve is in this range. Bearing replacement runs $300–$550. Written estimate before any work begins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Which areas of Southern California do you cover for commercial washer repair?</h3>
        <p>Same-day across <strong>Los Angeles, Orange, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside counties</strong>, Koreatown, Hollywood, Long Beach LA-side; Anaheim, Garden Grove, Costa Mesa OC; Thousand Oaks and Oxnard Ventura; Rancho Cucamonga, Riverside, Ontario IE. Eight service territories total. Speed Queen, Dexter, Maytag Commercial. BHGS #A49573.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do you repair coin-operated commercial washers?</h3>
        <p>Yes, the mechanical and electrical washer systems. Drain pump, motor, bearings, door lock, water inlet valve, control board. For coin acceptor and card reader electronics specifically, we assess on-site. The majority of coin-op failures are the washer, not the payment system, we'll tell you honestly which it is.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>My apartment building washer is not draining, can you come today?</h3>
        <p>Yes. We dispatch commercial washer calls same day across all five SoCal counties. Call {phone} and describe the machine and symptom. For multi-machine laundry rooms, tell us how many machines are affected so we can bring the right parts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Can you service multiple machines on the same visit?</h3>
        <p>Yes. For laundromats and multi-machine laundry rooms, we prioritize servicing all affected units on the same trip. Describe all machines needing service when you call, this lets us prepare for multiple repairs and minimize visits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How often should commercial washers be serviced?</h3>
        <p>Every 6 months for apartment building machines. Every 3–4 months for laundromat machines running 10–15 cycles per day. Regular maintenance catches drain pump wear, bearing degradation, and door boot deterioration before they become full failures.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do you repair Speed Queen, Dexter, and Continental Girbau washers?</h3>
        <p>Yes. Speed Queen is the most common commercial washer in SoCal, we carry Speed Queen parts on the van across all eight service territories. We also service Dexter, Maytag Commercial, Continental Girbau, UniMac, Wascomat, Electrolux Professional, and Huebsch.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Should I repair or replace my commercial washer?</h3>
        <p>Commercial washers last 10–15 years with proper maintenance. Under 8 years old, repair almost always makes sense, even a $400 repair on a machine generating $200+/week pays back in days. Over 12 years with motor or bearing failure, we'll give you an honest remaining-life assessment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Why is my commercial washer not draining or stuck full of water?</h3>
        <p>Not-draining is the number-one out-of-service call our techs run, usually a failed drain pump motor or a pump clogged with the lint, coins, and debris that high-volume machines accumulate, sometimes a blocked hose. The door stays locked because the safety interlock only releases when the drum is empty, which is why a load gets stranded inside. We test the pump, clear or replace it, drain the tub, and release the door. Quarterly pump cleaning prevents the repeat on laundromat machines. Same Day Appliance Repair, $120 commercial diagnostic, waived with repair.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What's the most expensive commercial washer repair, and how do I avoid it?</h3>
        <p>The rear drum bearing, and it announces itself with a grinding or rumbling on spin. Caught early, a bearing with tub seal runs $300–$550; let it seize and crack the inner race and you're into a $700-plus repair with tub damage. Call at the first grinding noise instead of waiting until the drum won't spin, and our 6-month preventive maintenance ($150–$280 per machine) includes a bearing condition check to catch it in the cheap window. Same Day Appliance Repair, $120 commercial diagnostic, waived with repair.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

